# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the Groundhog ASAN/UBSAN job
# (.github/workflows/groundhog-ci.yml, nostrc-qp24.15.2).
#
# Only leaks of libraries outside Groundhog whose objects Groundhog cannot
# free itself belong here, each with its bead; a leak in Groundhog code is
# fixed, never suppressed. LSan matches a function, source path, or module
# name in an allocation stack, but not the printed module+offset. The Linux
# sanitizer image/job installs matching libsecret debug symbols so the static
# handler can be matched without a module-wide suppression.
#
# nostrc-eixk6: libsecret 0.21.4 secret_collection_signal() hands a floating
# GVariant from g_variant_builder_end() to SecretCollection's
# handle_property_changed(), which neither sinks nor unrefs it. The only
# libsecret-specific function is static and requires matching debug symbols.
# Revisit when libsecret fixes this ownership error.
leak:secret_collection_signal

# nostrc-4bi6r / nostrc-ydtdf: Ubuntu Noble Pango 1.52.1 / Fontconfig 2.15.0
# process-exit font-map/config caches, using matching distro debug symbols.
# Repeated standalone AdwWindow + entry/button render/destroy (1 vs 100)
# retained 51,756 bytes / 1,786 allocations in both runs, not per-window growth.
# pangofc-fontmap.c:47-87 describes the font-map's pattern/fontset/font caches;
# match_in_thread (905) stores FcFontSetMatch in PangoFcPatterns.match, and
# load_fontset (2437) populates those cached fontsets/patterns. Reuses Grotto's
# source-proven exceptions; no allocation in Groundhog or its fixtures is exempt.
leak:match_in_thread
leak:pango_fc_font_map_load_fontset
# fcxml.c:3112: default-configuration patterns appended by FcParsePattern.
# A standalone mnemonic-button create/destroy control retained the same
# 320 bytes / 3 allocations for 1 and 100 buttons (with the test AT backend).
leak:FcParsePattern
# The fallback-font path is lazy: pangofc-fontmap.c:1256 renders a match and
# interns it in the same font-map cache via pango_fc_font_map_new_font, then
# destroys the temporary pattern. A repeated mixed-script/emoji render control
# with the three exceptions above retained exactly 31,877 bytes / 757 allocations
# for BOTH 1 and 100 windows. Only this library frame, not FcFontRenderPrepare.
leak:pango_fc_fontset_load_next_font
# Source: https://github.com/GNOME/pango/blob/1.52.1/pango/pangofc-fontmap.c
#         https://github.com/fontconfig/fontconfig/blob/2.15.0/src/fcxml.c
# Revisit these cache exceptions on dependency updates.

# nostrc-swjdk / nostrc-4bi6r: known per-operation upstream ownership bugs,
# NOT caches. The owner explicitly chose stock Ubuntu libraries plus these
# exceptions instead of privately patched libraries. Keep matching debug symbols
# installed: only named library allocation frames are exempt, never modules,
# allocators, generic GObject constructors or Groundhog frames. Remove each
# exception when Ubuntu ships the corresponding fix and its controls/full GUI
# set pass with that exception removed.
#
# GTK 4.14.5+ds (Ubuntu 24.04): mnemonic/shortcut relation lists leak when
# gtk_accessible_update_relation_value returns without an AT context. This
# fires with GTK_A11Y=none, and during non-accessible AdwActionRow construction
# even with the test AT backend. One vs 100 mnemonic buttons retained 24 vs
# 2,400 bytes: real per-operation growth. The combined 100-cycle mnemonic,
# shortcut and legal-section control leaked 44,700 bytes/1,900 allocations on
# stock Noble and zero after the former ownership patches (same font exceptions).
# GTK fixed list ownership in MR8277 (copy in collector, free in callers):
# https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gtk/-/merge_requests/8277
# https://github.com/GNOME/gtk/commit/3d11519f4295150267237dbf7161446a0e92ce15
# Source check: present in GTK 4.20.0, absent in 4.14.5. Delete these two list
# exceptions once the tested Ubuntu GTK contains that fix and controls pass.
leak:gtk_widget_list_mnemonic_labels
leak:gtk_shortcut_label_rebuild

# GTK 4.14.5+ds-0ubuntu0.10 also overwrites the owned move_focus_widget in
# _gtk_window_unset_focus_and_default when a focused widget is hidden and then
# unparented before after-paint. Prior ASan object tracing + GDB refcount watch
# identified seven retained AdwNavigationSplitView instances in onboarding.
# This is fixed upstream (g_set_object instead of g_object_ref assignment):
# https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gtk/-/merge_requests/9896
# https://github.com/GNOME/gtk/commit/a6e1c8a57e523fcf734d5b81a5e1d49c70457f4b
# Source check: fixed in GTK 4.24.0, not 4.22.0. Its retained-widget allocation
# stacks contain only generic GtkBuilder/GObject constructors, not the faulty
# reference operation; no broad constructor suppression is authorized here.

# libadwaita 1.5.0-1ubuntu2 (Ubuntu 24.04): breakpoint size allocation saves
# a snapshot in old_node; breakpoint_changed_tick_cb overwrites it without an
# unref, and disposal before the tick also omits cleanup. The retained GSK nodes
# repeat on breakpoint changes, not a renderer/process cache. The former narrow
# source patches made the GUI suites clean without any GSK suppression.
# Upstream tick fix is present in 1.5.5:
# https://github.com/GNOME/libadwaita/commit/b8f11388d8a34cad7880f02b7c3b9d92c7665a45
# Delete when Ubuntu has the node ownership fix (including teardown) and the
# breakpoint GUI paths pass without this exception. Exempt the specific owning
# libadwaita allocation operation, not generic GTK snapshot/GSK constructors.
# ASan malloc_context_size=64 is required: at the default depth, requests-GUI
# left 184 bytes/5 nodes with the owning libadwaita frame truncated from the
# allocation stacks; deeper capture passes with this same narrow exception.
leak:adw_breakpoint_bin_size_allocate

# libadwaita 1.5.0-1ubuntu2 (Ubuntu 24.04): add_legal_section duplicates
# copyright, but free_legal_section does not free it; repeats per legal section.
# Upstream fix (about-dialog AND about-window):
# https://github.com/GNOME/libadwaita/commit/6d91243bb52d81f61b4967d8ff1c610074be49a2
# Delete when the tested distro has that free and the legal-section control
# passes without this exception. Only the dialog API is exercised here.
leak:adw_about_dialog_add_legal_section
